{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:16.457258Z","id":"294289dc10bfafc9bb11e6226dd1167aae6de34137c567b0d8e8519aa4726727","body":{"detail":"inflateAtMost caps output bytes but not work. archive 4.5.2's Inflate builds a full 2^maxCodeLength HuffmanTable (32,768 entries at code length 15) for every dynamic block (codecs/zlib/_huffman_table.dart), and a dynamic block that declares one 15-bit literal and an immediate end-of-block costs about 12 input bytes and yields nothing. Measured with flutter test on macOS: 100,000 such blocks (1.2 MB) took 2.6 s in inflateAtMost; a 2.4 MB manifest.json entry made of them took 5.6 s in BundleReader.read before it failed bad_manifest. A 32 MiB .clax (the §6.1 cap) is about 70 s, and manifest.json is inflated before step 3, so no key is needed. apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart:87 awaits BundleReader.read on the UI isolate, so the app freezes for that long. Spec §9 T3 answers memory, not work.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"8222a2cd976c03edbf285cf7a258b550d8c5e0e77921f3fa85b1ea4a412272e8"},"suggested_fix":"Bound the work per entry: refuse an entry whose compressed size exceeds its cap (256 KiB for manifest.json, the manifest size for files and seed; the writer only deflates when smaller), and count deflate blocks in inflateAtMost, refusing more than max/1024 + 16 of them. Run BundleReader.read in Isolate.run so even a legal 32 MiB bundle does not stall frames.","summary":"A crafted deflate stream costs about 2 s of CPU per MiB with no output, before the signature check","tags":["security","review:BF","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:16.457924Z","id":"536fef68458dae52cc425a89ec3eb6dabd85f7b3f7c14ad9b9f993fc53f5e841","body":{"detail":"author.key = base64url of [1, 0 x 31] (the identity point) verifies the signature R = enc(aB), S = a mod L for every message, for any scalar a; a whole bundle with that key and a signature made without any private key reads through BundleReader.read. Under §6.5's first-use pin, every later bundle of that lineage under the same key is an update (with migrate.js), so anyone holding one copy can push updates to every install of it. Separately, cryptography 2.9.0's Ed25519Point.equals (lib/src/dart/ed25519_impl.dart:53-80) compares X twice and never Y, so verify accepts sB equal to the point (x, -y) of R + hA: with the identity key, R' = (x, -y) of aB and S = a mod L also verifies. Canonical S and y < p are checked, so the doc comment's 'strict' holds for encodings only. No forgery under an honest prime-order key follows from either, but the 'verified strictly' of spec §4.5 is not what this checks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"4060e12405c89ee248526d70ff5542f91a4cf63cbf5364169d9af12fb5bcca60"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse author.key and the signature's R when they are one of the small-order encodings (the 8 torsion points; libsodium's blocklist), and compare the encoded points rather than relying on Ed25519Point.equals, or use a verifier with strict semantics. Add a test with the identity key.","summary":"verifyManifest accepts a small-order author.key, under which anyone can sign any manifest; the library's point comparison checks only X","tags":["security","review:BF","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/manifest.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:16.457980Z","id":"032ebf00940c8741ee25aef909762cf175080f7d3adba00d8a040c44c0c374b1","body":{"detail":"Manifest.parse and _seedDocs (bundle_reader.dart:348-388) accept any JSON depth: capabilities {\"x\": 100,000 nested arrays} (200 KB, under the 256 KiB manifest cap) parses, signs and reads, and jsonEncode of the parsed value then throws StackOverflowError. The installer passes capabilities to the daemon unchanged and sends seed documents as JSON, so the failure lands there as an Error rather than a BundleError, after the person has seen the install sheet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":323},"content_hash":"cb7dc15e7a11670139c5bdafbccd1997b3353077ce84fa52bc879a952e88dea4"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse capabilities and each seed line's data deeper than a fixed cap (64 is ample) with bad_manifest / bad_seed, and test it.","summary":"capabilities and seed data have no nesting depth cap; re-encoding a deep value throws StackOverflowError","tags":["review:BF","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:16.458032Z","id":"4f56b9edfb640f68b0978b38569362812e3d46c8e7d4847a5707b3f581a8a0ee","body":{"detail":"_entries checks that cdOffset + cdSize equals the end record's offset, but not that the first local header is at 0, that each entry's data ends where the next local header starts, or that the central walk ends at cdOffset + cdSize. A valid bundle with 4 KiB of junk prepended (offsets shifted) reads, so a polyglot file passes, and Bundle.bytes, kept byte for byte for re-share, carries the junk. §4.1 says no other entry is allowed; the writer emits none of this.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":280},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"e0c8672ff7c2bd657bd0fb636796ba4e0d345daa40dc2e3f9aefaf169bbc76e6"},"suggested_fix":"Require local headers to be contiguous from offset 0 in central order and the central walk to end exactly at the end record.","summary":"Bytes before the first entry, between entries and after the last central entry are accepted","tags":["review:BF","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/manifest.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:16.458081Z","id":"754ef8db79e7f4cb89a3bbd594ca3df491a47caf535b87dbfa94cd0d1f03b8cf","body":{"detail":"A manifest with title 'Bank\\u202Egnp.exe\\n\\u0000' and author.name 'Alex\\u200B\\u0007' reads. §9 T10 rests on the sheets showing the name as the sender's claim beside the fingerprint; a right-to-left override, zero-width or newline makes that claim render as something else.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":365},"end":{"line":369},"content_hash":"bf44f67f526b699f28dbd9a8deb813828e974852af18d2db67850a5fad36bc47"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse C0/C1 controls, U+200B-U+200F, U+202A-U+202E and U+2066-U+2069 in title and author.name with bad_manifest.","summary":"title and author.name accept control and bidi-override characters","tags":["review:BF","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:56:44.443350Z","id":"087058cc74ccdac30aa4d1a62cdb87868f22b1c7ec20613ed2657f115b7fb4a4","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md §5.3 says an artifact_deleted event for <aid> removes its lineage entry and kept bundle, and §6.5 relies on it (deleting the app forgets the pin). The store offers forget(aid); the subscription to the daemon's events lives with the services or lib/app.dart, which must call it. Until then a deleted installed app's entry keeps matching its lineage in decide (lib/bundle/trust.dart), and a re-received bundle shows update/older/current against an app that no longer exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":277},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"7097996b39736523795bed06ecf7cf492eff2b00bf0f23b15429ea069dfb98c5"},"summary":"Nothing calls LineageStore.forget on artifact_deleted yet","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911194Z","id":"ab843a72851f426c7e74f379fea05164a19924d7e5bfd5e09d1175dd80a8dcda","body":{"detail":"_readRaw returns {} on FormatException or a non-object root, and put/forget/stopUpdates then write that map back over the file. One unparseable file (disk fault, a later format change read by an older build) silently loses every author lineage (the next export mints a new lineage, so recipients get a separate app instead of an update), every installed app's key pin and its released list, and leaves the kept bundles under bundles/ orphaned. It is safe for trust (a lost pin yields install as a new app, never an update of an existing one) but unrecoverable. The test at test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart:34 covers the empty read, not the write that follows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":303},"end":{"line":312},"content_hash":"450580fd998ab40d66bbc542c6858f9fb12ffd5f87f3b7ead8983a9a23c09148"},"suggested_fix":"On a parse failure, move the file aside (lineages.json.bad-<time>) before the first write, or refuse writes until it is dealt with; test put after a malformed file.","summary":"A malformed lineages.json reads as empty and the next write erases every lineage","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911229Z","id":"906f5ee561054885cb6c24e891dbe97e031ce6581559f198d15a258a4bbe2446","body":{"detail":"Callers read an entry, await other work, then put a derived entry: stopUpdates awaits entry() before put, and the updater (§8.2) will hold an entry across daemon calls before writing withRelease. A forget(aid) from artifact_deleted (087058cc) or another write landing in that gap is undone: the deleted app's entry and pin come back and keep matching its lineage in decide.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":263},"end":{"line":275},"content_hash":"ce5e73320f4a45e2b64a7d42d07acb3b4e3c6a2c121d7d97fd7fc7ca90a97922"},"suggested_fix":"Offer update(aid, LineageEntry Function(LineageEntry) change) that reads and writes in one synchronous step and does nothing when the entry is gone; use it in stopUpdates.","summary":"put is a blind overwrite, so a stale entry written after forget resurrects a deleted app","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:56:44.443540Z","id":"01dfd17f5af82d8954ea7e6ce56073e1c49306d39c3f9f11ae8686fa265ff4fa","body":{"detail":"§6.4 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md asks update to carry modified from §5.4, which needs the live version's content_sha256 and capabilities; the lineage store does not hold them. decide therefore takes an optional named live: {aid: ReleaseState}. The caller fetches the live state of local apps whose entry has the bundle's lineage (GET /api/artifacts/<aid>) and passes it; an app missing from live counts as modified, so the sheet offers 'Update (replaces your changes)' rather than silently replacing changes.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":112},"content_hash":"405021f6c18de569a9ca2ab9953c6cae2d2fcf759d16f1038a65abc33e7b7752"},"summary":"decide takes a live map beyond the spec's decide(bundle, store, ownKey)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911066Z","id":"47edb0d61239aff86bcd7fe7e7607c233e7ff3fa7eef7463c93cf5aa45ac04f7","body":{"detail":"decide answers own only when ownKey is non-null and equals author.key. When the caller cannot read the seed (macOS keychain prompt denied, BundleKey.existing throwing on a bad seed) and passes null, the person's own re-received bundle skips own, matches no installed entry, and lands on foreign at lines 137-139 against their own author entry: 'already installed from someone else', Install separately. ownKey adds nothing here: an author entry with the bundle's lineage and key exists only because this install signed with that key, so matching role author + lineage + key alone answers own without touching the keychain on every import (each read of a second keychain item is one more prompt per process on ad-hoc macOS builds). Also unhandled: an own-key bundle whose lineage has no local author entry (the author deleted the app) answers install and creates a role installed entry under the person's own key, so their next modified export forks instead of continuing the lineage. test/bundle/trust_test.dart has no case for ownKey null with an author entry, nor own key with no author entry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"3544ad15409787fc5ab990fe63164dc198271891a140e5bf0531d67ef9b47133"},"suggested_fix":"Match own on (role author, lineage, key) without ownKey, drop the keychain read from the import path, and add the two tests.","summary":"own needs ownKey from the keychain; without it the person's own app reads as foreign","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911152Z","id":"c9545e1b03adf56958e6f0e8b56422c5c3dd741096769b93de7fa830b2299c02","body":{"detail":"§6.4 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md defines forked as 'a local fork has the lineage and key as upstream'. Today only a fork sets upstream (§8.1 step 4 writes installed entries without it), so the result is right. If an installer ever copies a received bundle's forked_from into upstream, any bundle claiming forked_from of a lineage it does not own would make later genuine bundles of that lineage show 'You made <title> your own'.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"de87e4fd0f435fcf4a98685289879895881d0e9e0eca0ffbf30a202dca274390"},"suggested_fix":"Add e.role == LineageRole.author to the test and a case with an installed entry carrying upstream.","summary":"forked matches any entry with a matching upstream, not only a local fork (role author)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911364Z","id":"84e3adb08a80639c839903ba1b91e3a3c5db8b1bcc60779e59468db21e1ad8a9","body":{"detail":"With live omitted every update carries modified: true, so the sheet offers 'Update (replaces your changes)' / 'Keep mine' and nothing is replaced silently; current, conflict and older do not depend on it. The cost of a caller forgetting it is an unneeded question, and a 'Keep mine' answer that stops updates for an app that had no changes. An aid missing from live because the app was deleted (087058cc) also counts as modified and is offered an update; a caller that gets a 404 for the live state should forget the entry and decide again.","kind":"comment","references":"01dfd17f5af82d8954ea7e6ce56073e1c49306d39c3f9f11ae8686fa265ff4fa","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":112},"content_hash":"405021f6c18de569a9ca2ab9953c6cae2d2fcf759d16f1038a65abc33e7b7752"},"summary":"Reviewed: the live parameter is sound and safe by default","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:52.166741Z","id":"6e62095999009cfd7ec0153c12485ceeb097faea55e64b379298287af0972293","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"decide answers own on an author entry with the bundle's lineage and key, without ownKey; TrustDecision.mine marks a bundle signed by this install's key, so on install (own app deleted here) the installer can record role author. Evidence: flutter test test/bundle/trust_test.dart test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart test/platform/bundle_key_test.dart -> +36, All tests passed, including 'own without the keychain: an author entry with the lineage and key' and 'own bundle after deleting the app: install, marked as mine'.","supersedes":"47edb0d61239aff86bcd7fe7e7607c233e7ff3fa7eef7463c93cf5aa45ac04f7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:52.168166Z","id":"ca120bdacf365c99612f3651b7e1df6c764928e9cba207a7118c01c1ce595788","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"forked now requires a local entry with role author. Evidence: flutter test test/bundle/trust_test.dart test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart test/platform/bundle_key_test.dart -> +36, All tests passed, including the installed-entry-with-upstream case in 'forked: a local fork names the lineage and key upstream'.","supersedes":"c9545e1b03adf56958e6f0e8b56422c5c3dd741096769b93de7fa830b2299c02","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:52.169362Z","id":"c33955e691ef2d2b61728be7ae6055b510dad2f859c0480c7d186256cc41973d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"A damaged lineages.json reads as empty and sets LineageStore.damaged; the next mutation renames it to lineages.json.corrupt-<ms> (LineageStore.setAside) before writing, and a file that exists but cannot be read throws rather than being overwritten. Evidence: flutter test test/bundle/trust_test.dart test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart test/platform/bundle_key_test.dart -> +36, All tests passed, including 'a malformed file is set aside before a write, and reported'.","supersedes":"ab843a72851f426c7e74f379fea05164a19924d7e5bfd5e09d1175dd80a8dcda","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:52.170550Z","id":"9840d635877fa6901712061be9bfdd825d8d551e2519310301f35a4e06a7c49d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Mutations run under one lock; update(aid, change) re-reads under it; an artifact ID forgotten in this process drops later put/update/keepBundle. Evidence: flutter test test/bundle/trust_test.dart test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart test/platform/bundle_key_test.dart -> +36, All tests passed, including 'a forget during an update stays forgotten' (also a stale put after forget).","supersedes":"906f5ee561054885cb6c24e891dbe97e031ce6581559f198d15a258a4bbe2446","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:03.474157Z","id":"58cb2a380b64fc701c1c1987654703315d2193a2a84329fb48ace5e7df215fde","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"087058cc74ccdac30aa4d1a62cdb87868f22b1c7ec20613ed2657f115b7fb4a4","summary":"forgetDeleted(events, store, snapshots:) in apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart subscribes and calls forget (commit f1c07f346b12); Installer.open also forgets an entry whose app the daemon answers 404 for. Open until apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart subscribes it.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:03.474210Z","id":"a68839b90d671e20e615a886ae8e473aff8ce2f90fdfa7f3b3c811e0c959fc89","body":{"detail":"Section 8.4 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md restores a snapshot left by an update interrupted during its live migrate.js run, at the next start. recoverInterrupted does it and returns the notices to show once; apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart must call it after the daemon is up. Until then an interrupted update leaves the app on the new version with partly migrated documents and the snapshot file in <support>/snapshots/.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":335},"end":{"line":336},"content_hash":"01eaa0ad5e9be1a0acfc700fdbd66d856a68b1c489c59a9fe45abc92deff85f5"},"summary":"Nothing calls Updater.recoverInterrupted at the app's start yet","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:03.474246Z","id":"874d8a675377fe7ba911cf8c9c558a1ac81427968e8956d90211dd52e2484871","body":{"detail":"update takes no cancelled future; each step relies on the inspector's limits (runMigration total, runTests total, inspect settle). The progress sheet therefore has no Cancel. Acceptable while the sheet is modal and the limits are tens of seconds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":175},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"644b1a97a095e0d483b799cfa64b50297ebd45570f22864ad2d102586e1b7b3d"},"summary":"An update cannot be cancelled, and a hung inspector holds it for the inspector's own limits","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:33.912198Z","id":"20f451ffc7a5ea350da234ab2261d38e5b4ac66070a12f1f0f4b36986510a066","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"inflateAtMost caps deflate blocks at 2 + max/8192 and _Entry.inflate refuses a compressed size over max + 1 KiB; BundleReader.read runs files over 16 KiB on Isolate.run. The 20,000-empty-dynamic-block stream (1,061 ms uncapped) is refused: format_reader_test.dart \"many empty dynamic blocks are refused, not inflated\" (manifest.json: too_large) and \"a file over the inline size reads on another isolate\" pass. Residual: all files may declare 64 MiB in all, about 8,200 blocks or roughly 0.4 s, on the background isolate.","supersedes":"294289dc10bfafc9bb11e6226dd1167aae6de34137c567b0d8e8519aa4726727","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:33.913664Z","id":"5792f3a8cad21a6a92e85fbdffc95ba5c6fb575f8d9441b14d27b94643a57f91","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"_entries requires local headers end to end from offset 0 in central order with no local extra field, the last entry to end at the central directory, and the central walk to end at the end record. format_reader_test.dart group \"bytes outside the entries\" (before, between, after the last entry, after the end record) passes.","supersedes":"4f56b9edfb640f68b0978b38569362812e3d46c8e7d4847a5707b3f581a8a0ee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/manifest.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:33.914932Z","id":"5a18773b1474883727993e3d36dc5a52a7b1ac1896025b145cec04d6391cee41","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"withinJsonDepth (manifest.dart) caps capabilities and seed data at 64 levels: bad_manifest and bad_seed. format_reader_test.dart group \"JSON depth\" passes, including a 100,000-deep seed value refused without a StackOverflowError.","supersedes":"032ebf00940c8741ee25aef909762cf175080f7d3adba00d8a040c44c0c374b1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/manifest.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:33.916161Z","id":"39c87fcb0e21de199f60b960a15841819bf7a3aee2070a275dc8b3608dfab5ea","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Manifest refuses title and author.name holding C0/C1 controls, U+061C, U+200B, U+200E/F, U+2028-202E, U+2060, U+2066-2069, U+FEFF (bad_manifest); ZWJ and ZWNJ stay allowed. format_manifest_test.dart \"title and author name refuse hidden and direction characters\" passes.","supersedes":"754ef8db79e7f4cb89a3bbd594ca3df491a47caf535b87dbfa94cd0d1f03b8cf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:33.917357Z","id":"70c57ff7d801d5c528dce1a3873cfe50d3f7f0dabff99f79318c3ae7991d708c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"verifyStrict (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart) refuses a key with [8]A = identity and compares the re-encoded [S]B - [h]A with R byte for byte, no longer using cryptography Ed25519Point.equals. test/bundle/format_hash_signing_test.dart: \"a small-order author key is refused\" (identity and y=-1 keys), \"R is compared by its bytes, so (x, -y) of R fails\", \"RFC 8032 tests 1 to 3 sign and verify\", \"a BundleKey identity signs bundles that verify\" pass; flutter test test/bundle/: +126, all passed.","supersedes":"536fef68458dae52cc425a89ec3eb6dabd85f7b3f7c14ad9b9f993fc53f5e841","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:14:16.124660Z","id":"9f6768a77ec614682eafc45cf0b2903598c031609a869027c217b46e7dcc4eaa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _startBundles subscribes forgetDeleted(api.events(types: ['artifact_deleted']), _lineages, snapshots:) once the daemon is first up. Evidence: flutter test test/app_bundles_test.dart, 'a deleted app’s lineage is forgotten' passes (+3: All tests passed).","supersedes":"087058cc74ccdac30aa4d1a62cdb87868f22b1c7ec20613ed2657f115b7fb4a4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:14:48.411972Z","id":"cbe4d169083318f4afe9d62d1a721f821c1e086120128e3b414be2c63baa7006","body":{"detail":"Since f1c07f346b12, verifyStrict in apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart refuses an author.key on libsodium's has_small_order blocklist (smallOrderEncodings: the seven encodings, sign bit ignored) and an S not below L (a byte comparison), then calls cryptography 2.9.0's DartEd25519.verify. The BigInt verifier of f1c07f346b12 is removed. Tests in test/bundle/format_hash_signing_test.dart: RFC 8032 tests 1-3, the identity-key forgery passes the library alone but is refused, every blocklisted encoding refused with either sign bit, tampered signatures fail, a BundleKey identity verifies. The library's Ed25519Point.equals (X only) remains in the path: it also accepts [S]B = (x, -y) of R + [h]A. That point is -(R + [h]A) + T with T = (0, -1) of order 2, so with a key outside the blocklist an acceptance needs [-S]B = R0 + [h]A for R = R0 + T and h = H(R, A, M), the same equation as an ordinary forgery under A: not exploitable without the private key. It does make verification non-strict (a signature can be accepted that RFC 8032's cofactorless check rejects), so a second verifier may disagree on crafted signatures; no test, since showing it needs the point arithmetic this decision removes.","kind":"comment","references":"70c57ff7d801d5c528dce1a3873cfe50d3f7f0dabff99f79318c3ae7991d708c","summary":"Owner decision 2026-10-14: verify with an off-the-shelf implementation, no hand-written curve arithmetic","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.407896Z","id":"fd8f300ea918bb39e2a0c4eddc40f826cafdd8a215c1761fc213f8e05020ce10","body":{"detail":"Failure: an update bundle v2 with migrate.js whose declaration adds a capability or a net host, or changes the title or icon, and whose migrate.js fails on the live documents. _putBack (and recoverInterrupted at updater.dart:351-355) calls api.restoreVersion(aid, base), and docs/contract.md:190-197 says a restore makes version n's files the next version while \"the title, description, icon and capabilities stay as they are\". The app is then v1's files under v2's declaration and title, while the sheet says it is back on v1. Because its capabilities no longer equal the lineage's stored ones, LineageEntry.isModified (bundles spec section 5.4) reports it modified: the next opening of the same v2 shows \"You changed <title>\" with Update (replaces your changes) / Keep mine, and the export plan offers a fork. The test at apps/clax_app/test/bundle/updater_test.dart:187-230 checks only index.html and the version number. The rollback has to put back base's title, icon and capabilities too (for example PATCH the declaration after the restore, or roll back by a publish of base's files with base's title, icon and capabilities pinned to the published version), and SnapshotMeta (doc_snapshot.dart:45-80) has to carry them so recoverInterrupted can do the same. Spec section 8.2 step 7 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md:537-540) names only restoreVersion, so it has the same gap.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":446},"end":{"line":459},"content_hash":"84337ab232f50f491e86de3a4c7b586e2b63b6760ff20d7cd5e1043fe28b8518"},"summary":"A rolled-back update keeps the update's title, icon and capabilities: versions:restore puts back files only","tags":["review","bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.407984Z","id":"a0ba07f490e62b937895af0a1121f17506ff8da3d3fd63fa1da4b82e0bce093d","body":{"detail":"When a live migrate.js fails and _putBack also fails (updater.dart:449-459), update() returns UpdateRolledBack(restored: false) and keeps the snapshot for recoverInterrupted, with the documents half migrated. If the person tries the update again before the next start, snapshots.take (doc_snapshot.dart:126-145) writes the current, half-migrated documents over <aid>.jsonl and <aid>.json without checking DocSnapshots.has(aid), so the pre-update documents are gone for good. update() should refuse (or first run the pending restore) while a snapshot of the app is kept.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":247},"end":{"line":266},"content_hash":"0552a1497297400b3b7425f1e32dfe1c02364ab32ae7aa34b7159117433552d1"},"summary":"A new update overwrites a snapshot that was never restored, losing the only copy of the pre-update documents","tags":["review","bundles","data-safety","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.408028Z","id":"11521fd5c349fe965818b21c45f9466f50dec0d7aa15c7fab1d9c08742a8c8f2","body":{"detail":"A snapshot is kept across starts whenever a restore fails (updater.dart:361-363, and UpdateRolledBack(restored: false) at updater.dart:302-303). Meanwhile the app stays usable: after a failed _putBack it is on the update's version or on base, and the person keeps writing documents. At the next start that manages to restore, snapshots.restore sets every document back to the snapshot and deletes every document the snapshot lacks, destroying all of that work. The version is guarded by the content hash (updater.dart:352-355); the documents are not guarded at all. Matching the live version to the one the update published (record it in the meta after publish) and only restoring documents when the live version is still the update's or base, or telling the person and asking, would bound it. The matching by content hash itself is safe at start: two versions sharing the update's hash only differ in title or capabilities.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":335},"end":{"line":366},"content_hash":"87acb6d75b7709f1fe02c72eefb8094cf5954b3ba7baebac1b784346ddf592b1"},"summary":"recoverInterrupted restores the documents unconditionally, however long the snapshot was kept, overwriting everything written since","tags":["review","bundles","data-safety","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/doc_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.408076Z","id":"f779b16b715057e4e60ff8fbcb8fc024e4cfaee03d7223ce68ed02e771833bd5","body":{"detail":"take() writes <aid>.jsonl.tmp through an IOSink (flush() hands bytes to the OS, it does not sync them) and renames it, then the live migration starts within seconds. A device that loses power before writeback can come back with the renamed file empty or cut at a line boundary. recoverInterrupted then calls restore(), whose want map is empty or partial, and restore() deletes every document the snapshot lacks (doc_snapshot.dart:172-179). A cut mid-line throws in jsonDecode and is safe; an empty file or a cut on a newline is not. Sync the file before the rename (RandomAccessFile.flush, as _writeAtomic's flush: true does for the meta), and write the document count into the meta after the file so restore can refuse a short snapshot.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":145},"content_hash":"fb5c796f272913aed7e3fda17efea81a3299b3c9f5e4b4c5f88b6cdc8b8784c4"},"summary":"The snapshot file is renamed into place without an fsync; after a power loss an empty snapshot would make recovery delete every document","tags":["review","bundles","data-safety","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/doc_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.408113Z","id":"8bf6c0e77c100b66c93e58e2f3ef9d15f40a8c3fd79b386789d1d783a05b3e69","body":{"detail":"The writes list puts the snapshot's sets first and the deletes of documents migrate.js created last, in separate docs:batch calls of 50. A migrate.js that splits documents (or fails because it reached the quota) leaves the app near 5,000 documents; re-creating the documents it deleted before deleting the ones it made answers quota_exceeded (docs/contract.md:676), which restore() rethrows, so the rollback fails (UpdateRolledBack restored: false). Sending the deletes first is safe because the snapshot file stays until discard.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"21cb0251fcc7758e9d131da33f2824a7202d1b2d711fb3d0f396dd654b732dfa"},"summary":"restore() sends every set before any delete, so a migration that created many documents can push the restore over the 5,000-document quota","tags":["review","bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.408153Z","id":"d7de600d7c7fe74b21324e81c7e4bee67573f5b2cf12074607fc4a0176f01a2b","body":{"detail":"The trust decision is made when the bundle is opened (Installer.open, installer.dart:84-120); update() reads the entry and the live version again but does not check that the manifest's lineage and author key equal the entry's or that its version is above entry.version. If another update lands between opening a v3 sheet and tapping Update (two files opened in a row), the stale v3 publishes over v4: a downgrade, which bundles spec section 1 refuses. Re-running decide() (or those three comparisons) at the top of update() closes it cheaply.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":175},"end":{"line":199},"content_hash":"1a6d49e3f233a0a708b773ff270cee59f41b2cdc259016aec8f627738332023a"},"summary":"update() trusts its caller's earlier decision: it never re-checks the bundle's lineage, key and version against the lineage entry","tags":["review","bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.408191Z","id":"42639a0b114d7ead920dfada5f1d8b71d5df1d6def0cf135896778678dc10b81","body":{"detail":"_busy(aid) is read before the draft is made, but the update holds no claim on the app afterwards, so a queued change can start during the check or the live migration. A publish by it during the check is caught by if_version (409, refused). A publish during the live migration makes _putBack's restoreVersion(ifVersion: published) fail with 409 after the documents were restored, leaving the snapshot behind for the unconditional restore at the next start (see the concern on updater.dart:335-366). The updater should mark the app busy for its own duration so the agent's workers wait, as the spec's section 8.4 \"Nothing writes meanwhile\" assumes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":182},"content_hash":"439a22c2dc708a7247514249fccaab7f0a0c446bbe023cfef065fa871f5f30b8"},"summary":"The busy check runs once at the start; nothing stops an agent run on the app from starting during the update","tags":["review","bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.408318Z","id":"233efc67382cfda57825a37d2fa91dc085f85b80f38860ae43051321617fa265","body":{"detail":"Without migrate.js there is no snapshot; with it, the snapshot is discarded at updater.dart:305 before store.update. Clax dying between the publish (or the discard) and store.update/keepBundle (updater.dart:309-326), or store.update throwing (it is not caught, so update() throws despite its \"never throws\" contract), leaves the live version's content hash outside released: section 5.4 then calls the app modified, the same bundle opened again shows \"You changed <title>\", and a re-share sends the previous kept bundle. Recording the release (or a pending marker) before the publish, or reconciling at start, would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":298},"end":{"line":327},"content_hash":"73a26db9a58102f541060cf1e1e1a07e6bf9f5cf124bf472b185d3c0c9a48939"},"summary":"A crash or a store failure after publish leaves the lineage at the old version, so the updated app reads as modified","tags":["review","bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.408370Z","id":"49521d54529fd92a38e83550b41fcad8a1f833caed3bea066b875bdb4e2f962b","body":{"detail":"install() does not check that opened.decision.answer is install, foreign or forked, so a caller passing an update or own decision makes a second app on the lineage. And between createArtifact (line 133) and store.put (line 181) a crash leaves the bundle's app installed with no lineage entry: fromBundleOf (installer.dart:247-248) then answers false, so the agent of that app sees other apps' summaries and can read them, which threat T2 (bundles spec section 9) forbids. Writing a provisional entry with from_bundle true before createArtifact's result is used, or treating an app with a pending install marker as bundled, would keep T2.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":127},"end":{"line":196},"content_hash":"66f1455d84a05b0598197cb742dbabda33ef2962c3444c4a96b271f1e792ff68"},"summary":"install() accepts any decision, and a crash before the lineage entry is written leaves a bundled app with from_bundle unset","tags":["review","bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.408409Z","id":"26f5d1a2ea3a58655c1d190bb6ec5b9d8836758ab35fdef070efca53384cfafe","body":{"detail":"_check catches only InspectorError; anything else the inspector throws (a platform or state error) propagates out of update() past api.deleteDraft, breaking update()'s never-throws contract and leaving the draft for the daemon's hourly sweep (docs/contract.md:1873). A try/finally around _check would delete it on every path.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":236},"content_hash":"54d4dfbf7ba2ca456770fd5a1ebd5bf7ab0a4747ede102d2298383b881334c22"},"summary":"An exception other than InspectorError from the check skips deleteDraft and escapes update()","tags":["review","bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:16:02.803904Z","id":"f48525c40ed9fcfe470e1f1d5d205c57bb446b1eb1022c4856aeadd85a0aaed5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"70c57ff7d801d5c528dce1a3873cfe50d3f7f0dabff99f79318c3ae7991d708c","summary":"Checked the small-order blocklist (smallOrderEncodings, f1c07f346b12) against curve25519-dalek 5.0.0: the five canonical encodings equal the compressed EIGHT_TORSION points with the sign bit cleared, and dalek decompresses all seven listed encodings (p and p+1 included) to points with is_small_order() true. The only other non-canonical small-order y, p-1+p, does not fit in 255 bits, so the list is complete.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:17:56.833219Z","id":"87e80c03c77ebd0ba210d4d17d1aed2786bbfaec269ebe25f07ea886f7d46eb4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":335},"end":{"line":336},"content_hash":"01eaa0ad5e9be1a0acfc700fdbd66d856a68b1c489c59a9fe45abc92deff85f5"},"summary":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _startBundles (line 774) runs _recoverBundles once the daemon is first up, which awaits _updater.recoverInterrupted() (line 825) and shows one BundleNoticeSheet per RecoveredUpdate. Evidence: grep -n recoverInterrupted apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart prints '825: back = await _updater?.recoverInterrupted() ?? const [];'; flutter test (full suite) 1620 passed, 118 skipped. No app-level test covers the notices yet (record c8e36cbd).","supersedes":"a68839b90d671e20e615a886ae8e473aff8ce2f90fdfa7f3b3c811e0c959fc89","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.122929Z","id":"3e0bfc6b9972bdf65727440f0ee554570c2a0c46887af6ce2143c244a6572f05","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The rollback publishes base's files, title, icon and capabilities pinned to the update's version (Updater._rollBackVersion), and SnapshotMeta carries them for recoverInterrupted. Test updater_safety_test.dart \"a failed live migration puts back v1's files, title, icon and capabilities, so the app reads as unmodified\" asserts the title, icon, capabilities, content hash and isModified false. flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed. Spec §8.2 step 7 updated in f1c07f346b12.","supersedes":"fd8f300ea918bb39e2a0c4eddc40f826cafdd8a215c1761fc213f8e05020ce10","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.124601Z","id":"0fe68dca0104de382f8d61a0504d712fb44dad53c5bfad5eadcc623a99f15ebc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"DocSnapshots.take throws StateError when a snapshot is kept, and update() refuses while a snapshot or pending release of the app is kept. Test \"a failed rollback keeps the snapshot and refuses further updates\" asserts the kept file is unchanged after a second update and a second take. flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed.","supersedes":"a0ba07f490e62b937895af0a1121f17506ff8da3d3fd63fa1da4b82e0bce093d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.125950Z","id":"c42e46de23c61df443f998a138295ffbea03931a3c597c728dd3cb981acc2d8f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"recoverInterrupted restores only when the sidecar's published version is the live one with the update's hash and no restore failed before; otherwise it reports RecoveredUpdate(restored: false) and app.dart (f1c07f346b12) asks Restore or Discard (KeptUpdateSheet). Tests \"an interrupted update the app moved on from is kept for the person; Discard keeps the documents\", \"a failed rollback keeps the snapshot...\" and app_bundles_test \"an update kept at start asks Restore or Discard\". flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed.","supersedes":"11521fd5c349fe965818b21c45f9466f50dec0d7aa15c7fab1d9c08742a8c8f2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/doc_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.127275Z","id":"3de302ef0916f4af13d8bc5886551cc65d0b9fde41eea5dc5156b3cfd686bb99","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The snapshot and its sidecar are written through RandomAccessFile and flushSync (fsync) before the rename; the sidecar records the count after the file is in place, and read/restore throw SnapshotError, writing nothing, when the count is missing or differs. The directory is not fsynced (Dart has no call for it); a lost rename shows as a count mismatch. Test \"a snapshot whose count does not match is never restored\". flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed.","supersedes":"f779b16b715057e4e60ff8fbcb8fc024e4cfaee03d7223ce68ed02e771833bd5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/doc_snapshot.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.128604Z","id":"cd6a9eb78ab7d464c811ef62a0c6c2e838d17775659d2ee1c61d8b2de937926d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"restore() sends the deletes before the sets. Test \"restore deletes what the snapshot lacks before it sets\" asserts the op order delete, set, set. flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed.","supersedes":"8bf6c0e77c100b66c93e58e2f3ef9d15f40a8c3fd79b386789d1d783a05b3e69","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.129924Z","id":"a6cb8ab4971545b924b927f2c380f14ac2621390b893927b5039c90705ea8bc3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"update() checks lineage, key, role and a higher version at its start and again inside store.update, around the publish, under the store's lock. Test \"a bundle no longer above the lineage's version is refused right before the publish\". flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed.","supersedes":"d7de600d7c7fe74b21324e81c7e4bee67573f5b2cf12074607fc4a0176f01a2b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.131221Z","id":"27aa15efc7bbfab7ef46955971c7d3bdf079273ec1ee5eab8a1531fbed9e0281","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"update() runs inside hold (FeedbackWorker.hold, f1c07f346b12, wired in app.dart f1c07f346b12) and marks the app in Updater.updating for its whole run, released in finally. Tests \"the update holds the agent off and marks the app updating for its whole run, and releases both\" and worker_test \"hold waits for the app's running change and keeps its next one queued until the hold ends\". flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed.","supersedes":"42639a0b114d7ead920dfada5f1d8b71d5df1d6def0cf135896778678dc10b81","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.132500Z","id":"907f27f72fcb9b201d88726b9594db49577dc6901f10757c2f38b887b52aa615","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The release is written to <support>/updates/<aid>.json with the bundle before the publish; the lineage is written from it after, and recoverInterrupted finishes it when its hash is live. update() catches every error into UpdateRefused. Tests \"a release published before a crash is written to the lineage at start\" and \"a lineage write that throws is an outcome, not an exception\". flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed.","supersedes":"233efc67382cfda57825a37d2fa91dc085f85b80f38860ae43051321617fa265","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.133791Z","id":"5b82a907f935b49795bbf7b63fb96c429b95de05d95e86a654457a6bb3d19437","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"install() refuses decisions other than install, foreign and forked; writes the lineage entry right after createArtifact, before the content check and seeding; keeps <support>/installs/<lineage>.json meanwhile, during which fromBundleOf counts an app without an entry as from a bundle; recoverInstalls (called from app.dart, f1c07f346b12) deletes a cut-short install. Tests \"install records the lineage as from a bundle before the app is filled...\" and \"an install a crash cut short is deleted at start...\". flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed.","supersedes":"49521d54529fd92a38e83550b41fcad8a1f833caed3bea066b875bdb4e2f962b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.136435Z","id":"63cbf83a28ddf3d52732c263cd9a479f9b8ae45031084f6aa7ff94a17b9ef5b4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"_check runs in try/finally around deleteDraft and update() catches every error. Test \"an inspector that throws something else: the draft is deleted and update returns\". flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed.","supersedes":"26f5d1a2ea3a58655c1d190bb6ec5b9d8836758ab35fdef070efca53384cfafe","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:37:56.312034Z","id":"1b37aca93659025dc21973f64d37d1c3a36fc49a9ebf26ed4f8a7988ac5b04de","body":{"detail":"Since 20e1ed98c3fc (crates/clax-core/src/store/net_grants.rs access_in), every draft with draft_of inherits its live app's grants for hosts both declare. The updater's check (createDraft(of: aid) here, then _check runs migrate.js and tests/*.test.js in the inspect view) is such a draft: the update's code, before it is published, can send the copied documents to any host the owner granted the installed app. Bounded: same lineage and author key (_mismatch), only hosts the installed version declares and the owner granted, and a passing check publishes that same code anyway. The draft-net rule was written for the agent's render/test drafts (apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md); this path is not named in docs/contract.md or the bundles spec §8. If update checks should stay offline, the updater needs its own refusal (for example a draft flag the net route honours).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"b66db276da6513153b1596778001d1d7fa0baca89cf29fbd9eadecfdf3a4bffe"},"summary":"A bundle update's check draft now fetches under the live app's net grants, so the not-yet-published update's code runs with the person's document copy and network access","tags":["security","net","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:47:34.396877Z","id":"77500c5dcd5466536a734ed75cd4e63fbe6a22f960fc8d5f02a54a86446abae4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"1b37aca93659025dc21973f64d37d1c3a36fc49a9ebf26ed4f8a7988ac5b04de","summary":"Owner's decision (2026-10-14): no network in update checks. A bundle update's check draft must not use the live app's net grants; the agent's own change-run drafts keep using them.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:47:34.460423Z","id":"6e6b7f95b62c45d9c0084aa9639135f6e9754d95ed9b28354020658c04c2ac10","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: POST /api/drafts takes inherit_net (crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs), stored as artifacts.draft_inherit_net (migration 28), and net_grants.rs live_app_in gives a draft made with false no grants; the updater passes inheritNet: false (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart). Evidence: api_net::a_draft_fetches_under_its_live_apps_grants (offline draft gets not_granted for a host its app is granted) and net_grants::tests::an_offline_draft_or_one_whose_app_is_gone_reaches_nothing pass (cargo nextest -p clax-core -p clax-server: 1304 passed); flutter test test/bundle test/agent test/clax: 956 passed, updater_test asserts inheritNet false.","supersedes":"1b37aca93659025dc21973f64d37d1c3a36fc49a9ebf26ed4f8a7988ac5b04de","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T14:02:09.744920Z","id":"d5bac76d990b164c99f6ce80264b5ae2c69c0824fb56dc919d7dc3eee0bd8fd1","body":{"detail":"The padding changes which compressed bytes are accepted, not which content is: every inflated entry is checked after (files and seed.jsonl by exact size and sha256, manifest.json by the signature, manifest.sig by verifyManifest), so a cut-short or tampered stream passes only when it inflates to the signed bytes. A run of 8,000 raw deflate streams (archive's Deflate and dart:io ZLibEncoder(raw: true), 0 to 3,000 bytes of code-like, text and random bytes) read by the padded reader: 0 misread (76 misread unpadded); of 24,000 copies cut 1 to 3 bytes short, 6,305 inflated to something and 553 to the exact original, so a bundle whose stream is cut short can still read as whole, which zlib would refuse. format_reader_test.dart has a test for the short last code (line 207) but none for a cut-short entry.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":178},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"2ce61f5c752e16c28aaedcf18f94d212c3088871eed4cb34266efd38409908c1"},"suggested_fix":"Add a format_reader_test case: a deflated files/ entry with its last 1 and 2 bytes dropped (local and central sizes adjusted) is bad_file, and inflateAtMost of a cut-short stream is not the original for a stream that ends on a full byte.","summary":"No test pins that a deflate entry cut short is refused once inflateAtMost pads it with zeros","tags":["review","bundle","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T14:07:47.474762Z","id":"792b74aa208ade7232326171f410b7cf9e160af6582650deb12357e3df11031d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"format_reader_test.dart's group 'a deflated entry cut short or with bytes flipped' (f1c07f346b12) cuts each deflated entry of a signed bundle by 1 to 8 bytes and to half and flips each byte: files/ is bad_file, seed.jsonl bad_seed, manifest.json bad_manifest or bad_signature; inflateAtMost of every strict prefix of archive's and dart:io's raw deflate streams is null. Before f1c07f346b12 the manifest cases read as too_large and a prefix of Deflate('x' * 13) inflated to [120]; f1c07f346b12 refuses a stream whose decoding ends in the zero padding. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:bundle_format_reader_test //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze: both PASSED.","supersedes":"d5bac76d990b164c99f6ce80264b5ae2c69c0824fb56dc919d7dc3eee0bd8fd1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:44:54.616808Z","id":"832d388a1509f59b1cba59a65bc2e5b4e6de6c7fe3d0e67e9863f7fc865b174a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: Updater.update takes a cancelled future, passes it to every inspector run of the check, deletes the draft and answers UpdateCancelled before the publish; the progress sheet offers Cancel until the publish step. Tests 'a cancel during the check stops it: the draft goes, nothing is published' (apps/clax_app/test/bundle/updater_test.dart) and 'Cancel on the progress sheet stops the update and takes the sheet down' (apps/clax_app/test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart) pass (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_bundle_sheets_test //apps/clax_app:ui_bundle_flows_test //apps/clax_app:bundle_updater_test //apps/clax_app:ui_read_consent_dialog_test //apps/clax_app:platform_background_work_test //apps/clax_app:app_background_test //apps/clax_app:ui_change_sheet_test: all PASSED).","supersedes":"874d8a675377fe7ba911cf8c9c558a1ac81427968e8956d90211dd52e2484871","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:18:40.364565Z","id":"c86b122fbb096b679ca57d37d067ac31987d4a8b9d6cd395c52e3bef71e44b3e","body":{"detail":"Failure: an app whose live version carries an icon.svg published before f1c07f346b12 that clax_core::icon::problem refuses (a bare & in its <title>, an xlink:href without xmlns:xlink, an unknown entity: all read by package:xml and so passed by the old write_file check; or any icon an outside agent published, which nothing checked) installs a bundle update with a migration, and the live migration is interrupted or fails. _putBack (updater.dart:611) restores the documents from the snapshot first (line 615), then _rollBackVersion sends every file of version `base`, icon.svg included, to api.publish (line 678); publish::validate (crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs) refuses it with 400 invalid_icon. The app stays on the update's version with the documents in the base's shape, the snapshot is marked failed, and Restore (restoreKept, force) repeats the same refused publish. The core's own versions:restore (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs restore_version_async) skips the check, but the updater avoids it because it keeps the update's capability declaration.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":661},"end":{"line":690},"content_hash":"93b45bc517373791f9b190abfdbed80e66958dede09f0de5c4991f61519d0b36"},"suggested_fix":"Exempt a republish of history from the icon rule, e.g. skip the check when icon.svg's bytes equal a file the artifact already holds in an earlier version, or let the roll-back omit icon.svg when it equals the current version's and otherwise use versions:restore plus a capabilities update; pin it with an updater test whose base icon has <title>A & B</title>.","summary":"An interrupted update's roll-back republishes the base version's icon.svg through the checked publish route, so an older icon the core's rules now refuse leaves the app on the update's code with its pre-update documents","tags":["review","icon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:18:40.364641Z","id":"7345fbafa3184bb4553320c6d037a2266602cc41c0b3dad56eda77ccb5954b15","body":{"detail":"install() builds the createArtifact request from every file of the bundle (b.files, icon.svg included) and the updater's publish (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart:378) does the same; both are refused 400 invalid_icon and surface as 'The app could not be installed.' with the rule's sentence in details. The reader already has a drawable form: bundle_reader.dart:161 keeps cleanIcon's output as iconSvg, which drops what the subset leaves out. An icon the old Dart check passed (bare &, undeclared xlink prefix, unknown entity) therefore turns a working bundle into an uninstallable one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":190},"content_hash":"c31034d034a78eb5f8dc4c7fff0678072f52f34463932cf9ef7b23e704b9a161"},"suggested_fix":"Publish cleanIcon's output (or drop icon.svg when cleanIcon returns null) in place of the raw bytes, and add a bundle fixture whose icon has a bare & to the installer and updater tests.","summary":"Installing or updating from a bundle sends the bundle's icon.svg raw, so a bundle exported before f1c07f346b12 (or by another client) with an icon the core now refuses cannot be installed at all","tags":["review","icon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:35:10.330190Z","id":"489d988f36c3a9d5323530ba0f7e7c96303f0d8d7012276c322e3639ad0d5719","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The roll-back now restores the base through versions:restore with its title, icon and capabilities (the route takes them, checked as a publish's), so history is copied unchecked. Red first: the new updater_test 'a failed live migration rolls back to a base whose icon the icon rules now refuse' failed with restored false (invalid_icon from the publish); after f1c07f346b12 and f1c07f346b12 bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:bundle_updater_test passes, as does api_restore::restore_puts_back_a_declaration_with_the_files_unchecked.","supersedes":"c86b122fbb096b679ca57d37d067ac31987d4a8b9d6cd395c52e3bef71e44b3e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:35:10.636113Z","id":"2dcd9ff86a6e3a26d8fbddc84d8e1ff3504e20c0341fe75754ee8aac5e59aa05","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"PublishedFiles.of publishes a refused icon.svg as cleanIcon writes it when that passes iconProblem, else leaves it out, and Installed.iconChange / UpdateLanded.iconChange and the version note say which; a passing icon goes byte for byte. FakeClaxApi now refuses bad icons as the daemon does. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:bundle_installer_test //apps/clax_app:bundle_updater_test pass (cleaned, left out, byte for byte; an update cleaned, then one left out).","supersedes":"7345fbafa3184bb4553320c6d037a2266602cc41c0b3dad56eda77ccb5954b15","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:12.352280Z","id":"511c2132a58b64276d4ec513cce25983e035b22d7302b752612355f55de71e7a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":522},"end":{"line":523},"content_hash":"01eaa0ad5e9be1a0acfc700fdbd66d856a68b1c489c59a9fe45abc92deff85f5"},"summary":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _startBundles (line 774) runs _recoverBundles once the daemon is first up, which awaits _updater.recoverInterrupted() (line 825) and shows one BundleNoticeSheet per RecoveredUpdate. Evidence: grep -n recoverInterrupted apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart prints '825: back = await _updater?.recoverInterrupted() ?? const [];'; flutter test (full suite) 1620 passed, 118 skipped. No app-level test covers the notices yet (record c8e36cbd).","supersedes":"87e80c03c77ebd0ba210d4d17d1aed2786bbfaec269ebe25f07ea886f7d46eb4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:14.544903Z","id":"61db4332282defb528cd3afcf8c3f3c93ff4860463e521c58a6bdc72bc2f8065","body":{"detail":"clax_core::icon::problem refuses bytes that are not UTF-8 before anything else (crates/clax-core/src/icon.rs problem: \"it is not UTF-8\"), and FakeClaxApi._checkIcon does the same with a strict utf8.decode. PublishedFiles.of instead decodes with allowMalformed: true, which turns a bad byte into U+FFFD, a character iconProblem accepts; why is null, the bundle's raw bytes are published, and createArtifact or publish answers 400 invalid_icon. Inputs: a bundle whose icon.svg is a valid icon apart from one non-UTF-8 byte in text, for example <title>Caf\\xe9</title> written as Latin-1 by another client or a build before the icon rules. That is the failure f1c07f346b12 set out to remove (a bundle icon the daemon refuses failing the install). installer_test covers a bare &, a non-square viewBox and a passing icon, none of them undecodable.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":94},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"5435beca7503ad0e2ba3035a25a779fd6fbaae5fdbff990476ffadfae102b581"},"suggested_fix":"Decode strictly; on a FormatException treat the icon as refused with not_xml (\"it is not UTF-8\"), then clean the lossy decode or leave it out as for any other refused icon. Add an installer_test and an updater_test vector with a Latin-1 byte.","summary":"PublishedFiles.of reads a bundle's icon.svg with utf8.decode(allowMalformed: true), so an icon that is not UTF-8 but otherwise passes goes out byte for byte and the daemon refuses the whole install or update with invalid_icon (not_xml)","tags":["review","bundles","icons","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:25:59.108551Z","id":"a91bf1815be1a9752808883db7aef974dab7c2b220b2dabfb72a2aa5c2bec5c8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: PublishedFiles.of checks icon bytes with iconBytesProblem (the core's order: size, UTF-8, then iconProblem) and cleans iconText's reading (Latin-1 when not UTF-8): <title>Caf\\xe9</title> is redrawn, an icon that fails either way is left out. FakeClaxApi._checkIcon and the bundle reader use the same helpers. installer_test's two Latin-1 tests and updater_test's failed before (400 invalid_icon / 'The app could not be installed.') and pass now; bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:bundle_installer_test //apps/clax_app:bundle_updater_test //apps/clax_app:agent_icon_svg_test //apps/clax_app:agent_icon_fixtures_test pass.","supersedes":"61db4332282defb528cd3afcf8c3f3c93ff4860463e521c58a6bdc72bc2f8065","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:53:57.725541Z","id":"4c69415b009ea616bc8ce9aaf4f4deb3432fccacacc8ba68ddddf560529366a8","body":{"detail":"keepBundle, bundleBytes and the lineage file's read run on the caller's isolate, the UI isolate for installs, updates and exports; with them the per-file sha256Hex of an install's or an export's files (lib/bundle/installer.dart:127, lib/bundle/exporter.dart:203) and the publish request's JSON (HttpClaxApi.publish, lib/clax/http_api.dart:135-148, with lib/clax/models.dart:226 base64-encoding each binary file) are made there too. They run on a person's install, update or export, not while a page loads.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":319},"end":{"line":401},"content_hash":"578a4be1ddf5e7976750b260ae7715ffdb6e4f8b60a7825f51cadaff9375d539"},"suggested_fix":"Do the bundle file IO with dart:io's async calls and the hashing and the request's encoding on a background isolate (Isolate.run past offloadBytes, lib/platform/offload.dart).","summary":"A kept bundle (up to the 32 MiB a .clax may be) is written with writeAsBytesSync(flush: true) and read with readAsBytesSync on the UI isolate","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:50:08.049882Z","id":"7d8e6578dea6b9e040fbfa05738b9605a146f908d772b3cb3ea2c9ab46eb2c5d","body":{"detail":"Updater.update with a BundleOrigin naming the entry's link takes a bundle under any key, and _applyPending (updater.dart:484) writes the release into the lineage entry with copyWith, keeping LineageEntry.link unchanged: link.baseRemoteVersion and link.takenBundleVersion still name the public version taken before. Until the caller moves them, syncState (lib/remote/sync_state.dart) still reports the head just taken as updateWaiting for an author whose base did not move. LineageEntry.key also stays the first signer's, so a file of the lineage signed by the editor's key and opened without an origin is decided foreign.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":259},"end":{"line":282},"content_hash":"d91bc1f86f6f85b86439a891752b094ebabf4530843cb21c95f993f6ff17345a"},"summary":"A linked update leaves the AppLink's base and taken bundle version, and the entry's key, as they were","tags":["remote","bundles","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:50:08.049976Z","id":"2e728f7ddef454e9376df12811640c0b8bbfc33a179bee338048757954fab00b","body":{"detail":"The linked row answers update, current, conflict or older, so the sheets that switch exhaustively on TrustAnswer (lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart:1289, lib/home/home_install.dart:134) keep working; TrustDecision.linked says the answer came from that row. A separate enum value would force every switch to handle it and then map it to those four anyway.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"a6f52b21a780b4ecf337f387b9a9e36d7b8365776a7510767f4cf114ef6db486"},"summary":"TrustAnswer.linked as an enum value","tags":["revisit:a sheet must show a linked answer differently from the key-based one","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:55:08.202599Z","id":"6ac33b075d79df9f5e616ad0739b74a530e53b6157c1895a2e9f53150c99e63d","body":{"detail":"install(opened, link: l) stores l as LineageEntry.link whether or not opened.origin names it (BundleOrigin.names), and also when opened.origin is null (a .clax opened from a file). The link is what the linked row of decide (lib/bundle/trust.dart:112-118) and Updater._mismatch (lib/bundle/updater.dart:496-507) later trust to take bundles of that lineage under any key. Inputs: a caller passing the link of the page it is showing while installing bytes opened from Files or the share sheet; the app is then linked to a public copy it was never fetched from. Nothing in the installer refuses the mismatch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":225},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"f8101f3f7b1f1c6ebc6c0295a813ade1f3a0954d079b209a0999e5ae956df502"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse (BundleFailure) a link that opened.origin does not name, or derive the link's remote origin and artifact ID from opened.origin and take only the role, base and switches from the caller; add an installer_test for a link with no origin and one naming another copy.","summary":"Installer.install writes any given AppLink into the new entry without checking it against OpenedBundle.origin","tags":["review","trust","remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:55:08.203345Z","id":"0da5831afdd65723d4b15c25a49e85daa7dc7ca0cb1e6ef7fb5d324c9d920bfa","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md §5.8 says that on the linked row the signature is still verified and the signer's fingerprint is recorded with the release. _applyPending writes the release with withRelease and copies the new signer's name, but neither the release nor the entry keeps the signing key or its fingerprint, so after an editor's update nothing local says which key signed the version now live (see also record 7d8e6578dea6 on the entry's key).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":484},"end":{"line":507},"content_hash":"fe8118d1a952f44b977df7a91a68e89e68ab47a9d680f0805ba75b7f2a5a8613"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the signer's key (or keyFingerprint) per released version in LineageEntry, written by _applyPending and Installer.install, and show it where the release is shown.","summary":"A linked update records no signer fingerprint with the release","tags":["review","trust","bundles","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:10.052892Z","id":"b28bc41dc05df4dc41a56cc42531c8cc76c919127b137a4b541071e6750355fe","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f8cf5de17","summary":"Installer.install now throws BundleFailure('install', 'This app was not got from the public copy it would be linked to.') unless OpenedBundle.origin names the given link; the new case in test/bundle/installer_test.dart passes, and //apps/clax_app:bundle_installer_test PASSED under just test-affected at 0cca94805.","supersedes":"6ac33b075d79df9f5e616ad0739b74a530e53b6157c1895a2e9f53150c99e63d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:15:17.638083Z","id":"077aa123b55ca924f44071a6bd5b68b16c65c5b1d7c12e523f850c26a67ef711","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7d8e6578dea6b9e040fbfa05738b9605a146f908d772b3cb3ea2c9ab46eb2c5d","summary":"Since e45f2731e the link moves: Updater._applyPending sets baseRemoteVersion (never back) and takenBundleVersion when the pending release came from the linked copy (the origin is kept in updates/<aid>.json, so recovery moves it too), and BundleFlows passes the bundle's origin to Updater.update. test/remote/checker_test.dart 'a landed automatic update moves the link, and the app reads live' fails without it (Expected 2, Actual 1). LineageEntry.key still stays the first signer's.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:35:16.035750Z","id":"8392f27fc779cc1e34811eac6dc3636f5e86f4f653a791f993acdfe4ff725125","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0da5831afdd65723d4b15c25a49e85daa7dc7ca0cb1e6ef7fb5d324c9d920bfa","summary":"Since c01f06ddd a landed update records its signer with the release as LineageEntry.liveFrom (key, name or fingerprint, origin, publishing account), written by Updater._applyPending from the pending file; test/bundle/updater_test.dart 'an editor’s update is who published the live version, and the next change asks about them once' checks it. The release list itself still carries no signer per hash.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102563Z","id":"cd0e070c5039e91bae46b683bfef514e76f08aabeed6fdc1f773a13e748829a7","body":{"detail":"The data tools refuse every read of another app for an app whose code came from someone else's bundle (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart:64-79, fromBundleOf). An author app that takes an editor's bundle through the linked Update, a web-made head through Take theirs, or a Combine records LineageEntry.liveFrom but leaves fromBundle false, so its next run may read the person's other apps (after the owner's per-app read consent), unlike an installed copy of the same code.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":451},"end":{"line":458},"content_hash":"3c868d3ae36c156fc422ae2bf8a9cd57fc2a2b5147b947a061d60cd7b057caf3"},"suggested_fix":"Treat an entry whose liveFrom is someone else's (not ownKey, not the person's account) as fromBundle in fromBundleOf, or set fromBundle where liveFrom is set.","summary":"Code another person wrote that an app made here took in keeps fromBundle false, so its runs may read the person's other apps","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102772Z","id":"f58fa140e721c9a89c8dfb97203e0648a16716ee43e7747962f889231356ed10","body":{"detail":"all() and entry() call _readRaw (file.readAsBytesSync and jsonDecode of the whole file) and writes fsync (lines 419-422). This branch reads it per held-reply lookup (LinkedAppHooks.heldReply via _publicVersion, apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart:1467), per check of each linked app on every foreground (LinkedChecker), per run gate (AuthorTrust.authorOf reads all()), and per publish several times; the file grows with every AppLink. The app's rule is that the UI isolate only draws.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":302},"end":{"line":310},"content_hash":"1797dd4f682c4bec768d5be871648b19e9e4de2add05690cc932f090a801171d"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the parsed map in memory behind the store's lock and write it with async IO, or move the store behind the core client off the UI isolate.","summary":"Every lineage read is a synchronous read and decode of lineages.json on the UI isolate, now on hot paths","tags":["review","ui-thread","perf","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102853Z","id":"6f11a208cd237a031d5e3dc416ff2b375c116edee35f7899adc2cfcf24a51286","body":{"detail":"_writePending writes the bundle (up to 32 MiB) with _syncWrite (writeFromSync, flushSync), and _applyPending reads it back with readAsBytesSync before LineageStore.keepBundle writes it again synchronously. Updates were run only from the update sheet before; LinkedChecker now starts them itself at onForeground (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/checker.dart _autoUpdate, via AppRoot's runUpdate), beside the first frames after the app returns.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":524},"end":{"line":630},"content_hash":"e6d225ae6573d6b1e3d5896d4a7277fb064ce16eb00999943f6bd3573e79300a"},"suggested_fix":"Use async file IO (or Isolate.run) for the pending bundle and the kept bundle.","summary":"Automatic updates write and fsync the whole bundle synchronously on the UI isolate when Clax comes to the front","tags":["review","ui-thread","perf","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T05:35:13.889776Z","id":"3e61afc4f3a71b2eafce97d155be4a530a73169a685c4d10b23b43b00778b737","body":{"detail":"Installer.install approves the created version's pending capabilities (limited to what the bundle declares) whatever the caller showed. apps/clax_app/lib/remote/puller.dart:223 installs without any sheet when its confirm is null, so that path approves what no person saw. Updater.update approves only when confirm is non-null, so its callers carry the same duty in the opposite direction.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":236},"end":{"line":330},"content_hash":"78583f88ed28c1afecc015edc63418b74e0c8d077e4c17a8f5b8760a840c2a58"},"suggested_fix":"Make the install take the consent explicitly (a required confirmed flag or an approve: parameter) so a caller that showed no sheet cannot approve by default.","summary":"Installer.install and Updater.update do not enforce consent themselves: approval relies on every caller having shown a sheet","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
